From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:27:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): serve lean session item pages and a per-item
 read

Tool output dominates the bytes of a session items page: on a transcript
with realistic tool results (4-5 KB each) a 20-item page is ~40 KB and a
200-item page ~500 KB, while the web renders every tool row collapsed and
never shows most of those bytes. That is why the chat can afford only a
small history page and holds a narrow window of the session.

Add `tool_output=preview` to `GET /v1/sessions/{id}/items`: each
`function_call_output` longer than 400 characters comes back with only
that head plus `output_length` and `output_truncated=true`; shorter
outputs and every other item are unchanged, and the default stays
`full`. Add `GET /v1/sessions/{id}/items/{item_id}` so a client can
fetch one item in full when the reader expands it (queued inputs stay
hidden, as in the list). Put both reads on a `GZipFileContentRoute`
router, like the workspace-file reads: a page of tool output compresses
about 5x, and a 200-item preview page gzipped is ~14 KB.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/lean-history-items; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3abfcc5128b8bc551900ad1e5eded5c2789e61f6)
